219 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 195 0 R
/E (The year 2025 marked five years of growth and impact for WeCare Youth Organization, providing an opportunity to consolidate its achievements and expand its influence in advocacy and policy engagement at both national and county levels.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
220 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 195 0 R
/E (During the year, the organization strengthened its role in governance and policy influence by submitting 10 policy memoranda and participating in 5 parliamentary committee engagements, with many recommendations adopted by relevant authorities.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
221 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 195 0 R
/E (WeCare also expanded its youth engagement programs by extending its reach to Masinde Muliro University of Science and Technology \(MMUST\) and Jaramogi Oginga Odinga University of Science and Technology \(JOOUST\). This increased the number of Transparency and Integrity Clubs to four, developed in partnership with Transparency International Kenya to promote youth leadership and civic participation.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
222 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 195 0 R
/E (Additionally, the organization received its first institutional grant through the TUNU Project, which will strengthen youth engagement initiatives and support governance participation through university-based clubs.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
223 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 195 0 R
/E (Through strengthened partnerships with organizations such as Konrad Adenauer Stiftung Kenya, Transparency International Kenya, World Vision, Community Led Solutions, the National Democratic Institute \(NDI\), and CIVICUS, WeCare continued to expand its impact in youth advocacy and governance.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
